{
  "summary": "Adds script and functional test cases covering the 1,000-element stack size limit boundary during P2SH execution. It tests that when a scriptSig leaves 1,000 items on the stack, the 20-byte hash push during scriptPubKey evaluation triggers a STACK_SIZE failure, whereas leaving 999 items succeeds. It also adds a spender to the taproot functional test so the transaction can be exported into QA script test assets.",
  "problem": "Existing test vectors omit coverage for scriptSigs that push the stack to the 1,000-item limit before the P2SH scriptPubKey runs. As a result, non-compliant Bitcoin implementations that check redeemScript hashes directly without executing the scriptPubKey against the stack can pass all existing test vectors despite erroneously accepting invalid 1,000-item spends.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: \"An implementation that checks the redeemScript hash without running the scriptPubKey accepts the 1,000-item spend. No existing vector leaves the scriptSig at this boundary, so such an implementation can pass every row.\"",
    "PR description: \"These were discovered by finding gaps in an alternate implementation (rbitcoin)\""
  ],
